(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// The program's CAFs given up when no live code can reach them (smalls-1123, unpack_sums_6; doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md,"] [11 1 "// \"As built: the program's CAFs collected\"). GHC's collector keeps a CAF only while a live closure's or frame's SRT names it, so"] [12 1 "// a top-level list the program floated out (unpack_sums_6's `makeUnlayered magnitude`, a CAF at -O0) is freed cell by cell as"] [13 1 "// its consumer walks it. hsi's globals are Go roots, so an evaluated CAF kept its whole value for the run (10 million"] [14 1 "// cells, 15 GB). Now, when the Go heap has grown past a threshold, the machine marks what its threads, stable pointers, weak"] [15 1 "// pointers and the C API reach (rts.go's marker, following each closure's code to the globals it names, but not the code of"] [16 1 "// a thunk under evaluation: GHC's blackholed thunk has no SRT) and reverts every evaluated CAF of the program's own modules"] [17 1 "// (unit main) that the mark did not reach: unevaluated again, its value left to Go's collector. A reverted CAF entered again"] [18 1 "// is evaluated again, as GHCi's revertCAFs does; by the mark no live code can enter it. The libraries' CAFs (stdout and the"] [19 1 "// other handles, the RTS's closures Go names by name) are never reverted. HSI_CAF_GC=0 turns it off; HSI_CAF_FLOOR_MB sets"] [20 1 "// the floor."] [22 1 "// cafRec is a CAF of the program: its global, its thunk and its code."] [29 1 "// cafFloor is the Go heap's size below which no collection of CAFs runs (by default); cafEvery the slices between two looks"] [30 1 "// at the heap."] [36 1 "// noteCAF records a top-level thunk of a module of the program's own unit."] [44 1 "// cafCheck is run between slices by the outermost scheduler: every cafEvery slices it reads the heap's size, and past the"] [45 1 "// threshold (cafFloor, then twice the heap at the last collection) collects the program's unreachable CAFs."] [71 1 "// collectCAFs marks what the machine's roots reach (conservatively: every thread not done, every weak pointer's key, value"] [72 1 "// and finalizers, the stable pointers, the C API's objects, the static pointer table) and reverts the program's evaluated"] [73 1 "// CAFs the mark did not reach. It returns how many."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis []} (go/file "cafgc.go" :imports [


